{"id":"v5","level":4,"levelName":"The verb system","n":6,"of":10,"title":"Doing it to yourself","titleHe":"בִּנְיַן הִתְפַּעֵל","goal":"Recognise hitpa'el — and the letter-swap that hides it.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"הִתְפַּעֵל is reflexive: the action comes back on whoever does it. Present begins מִתְ, past begins הִתְ."},{"type":"binyan","he":"הִתְפַּעֵל","en":"hitpa'el","note":"Reflexive — the action comes back on the one doing it.","verb":{"root":"ל־ב־ש","inf":"לְהִתְלַבֵּשׁ","en":"to get dressed"},"tense":"present","rows":[{"label":"masculine singular","he":"","form":"מִתְלַבֵּשׁ"},{"label":"feminine singular","he":"","form":"מִתְלַבֶּשֶׁת"},{"label":"masculine plural","he":"","form":"מִתְלַבְּשִׁים"},{"label":"feminine plural","he":"","form":"מִתְלַבְּשׁוֹת"}]},{"type":"text","body":"When the root starts with a hissing letter — ס, שׂ, שׁ, צ, ז — that letter swaps places with the ת, because the two are awkward to say in the other order."},{"type":"table","caption":"The swap","head":["expected","actual","meaning"],"rows":[["מִתְסַכֵּל","מִסְתַּכֵּל","looks at"],["מִתְשַׁמֵּשׁ","מִשְׁתַּמֵּשׁ","uses"],["מִתְצַעֵר","מִצְטַעֵר","is sorry"]]},{"type":"tip","body":"With צ the ת also hardens to ט — מִצְטַעֵר, not מִצְתַּעֵר. It's the one form worth memorising outright, because מִצְטַעֵר is how you apologise."}],"vocab":[{"he":"מִתְלַבֵּשׁ","en":"gets dressed","translit":"mitlabesh"},{"he":"מִתְעוֹרֵר","en":"wakes up","translit":"mit'orer"},{"he":"מִסְתַּכֵּל","en":"looks at","translit":"mistakel"},{"he":"מִשְׁתַּמֵּשׁ","en":"uses","translit":"mishtamesh"},{"he":"מִצְטַעֵר","en":"is sorry","translit":"mitsta'er"},{"he":"מִתְגַּעְגֵּעַ","en":"misses, longs for","translit":"mitga'age'a"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["requests","reading, a call","gets dressed","strange"],"correct":2,"prompt":"מִתְלַבֵּשׁ","translit":"mitlabesh"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["all the more so","nature","wakes up","yes"],"correct":2,"prompt":"מִתְעוֹרֵר","translit":"mit'orer"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["that is to say","looks at","baby","deed, work"],"correct":1,"prompt":"מִסְתַּכֵּל","translit":"mistakel"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["uses","thanks, admits","hard, difficult","lives, resides"],"correct":0,"prompt":"מִשְׁתַּמֵּשׁ","translit":"mishtamesh"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["pleasant","is sorry","what (Aramaic)","book"],"correct":1,"prompt":"מִצְטַעֵר","translit":"mitsta'er"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["opinion","part, portion","misses, longs for","mouth"],"correct":2,"prompt":"מִתְגַּעְגֵּעַ","translit":"mitga'age'a"},{"type":"choice","q":"Which binyan is this verb in?","options":["הִפְעִיל","פִּעֵל","נִפְעַל","פָּעַל"],"correct":2,"prompt":"נִכְנָס"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “is sorry”?","options":["יְרָקוֹת","חַם","אֵשׁ","מִצְטַעֵר"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “gets dressed”?","options":["אַף אֶחָד","בְּיוֹתֵר","מִתְלַבֵּשׁ","דּוֹדָה"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"Why is it מִשְׁתַּמֵּשׁ and not מִתְשַׁמֵּשׁ?","options":["The ש and the ת swap places","It's an unrelated irregular verb","The root has four letters","It's a different binyan"],"correct":0,"why":"Roots beginning with a sibilant swap that letter with the ת of the prefix."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “uses”?","options":["מַיִם","חֲמִשָּׁה","אִיָּר","מִשְׁתַּמֵּשׁ"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “looks at”?","options":["קוֹל","מֶרְחָק","בְּמֶשֶׁךְ","מִסְתַּכֵּל"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"מִתְעוֹרֵר","translit":"mit'orer","en":"wakes up"},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["מִצְטַעֵר","מִשְׁתַּמֵּשׁ","מִתְעוֹרֵר","מִסְתַּכֵּל"],"correct":3,"say":"מִסְתַּכֵּל","he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["מִתְלַבֵּשׁ","gets dressed"],["מִתְעוֹרֵר","wakes up"],["מִסְתַּכֵּל","looks at"],["מִשְׁתַּמֵּשׁ","uses"],["מִצְטַעֵר","is sorry"]]},{"type":"type","q":"Write “gets dressed” in Hebrew","answer":"מִתְלַבֵּשׁ","hint":"mitlabesh"}]}